During the spike, the certificate service consumes the CDC topic of the enrollments table directly. A change event (simplified):

{ "op": "u",
  "before": { "id": "e_9902", "status": "active", "completed_at": null, "internal_note": null },
  "after":  { "id": "e_9902", "status": "completed", "completed_at": "2026-10-22T09:14:03Z", "internal_note": null },
  "source": { "table": "enrollments", "lsn": 81234560 } }

Consumer code:
if (msg.after?.status === "completed" && msg.before?.status !== "completed") issueCertificate(msg.after.id);

The enrollment team plans this migration for next week, with no change to any event contract they publish:
ALTER TABLE enrollments RENAME COLUMN status TO state;

Statement: "After this migration the certificate service stops issuing certificates, even though the enrollment team changed no event they own."
